untry>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, MOTONOBU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO YOSHIHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA MOTONOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, MOTONOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>First and second reflecting faces (2, 3) adapted for forming an image of an object on an image plane (4) and having non-axially symmetrical shape are arranged eccentrically to each other in order in the direction of the travel of light from the object. The cross sections of the first and second reflecting faces (2, 3) cut by a plane including the center of the image plane (4) and the vertexes of the reflecting faces (2, 3) are concave. Therefore, light from the object is guided to the image plane (4) without being blocked, and the image is good, thus providing a wide-angle, high-performance reflection optical device.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Une première et une deuxième faces réflectrices (2, 3), conçues pour former une image d'un objet sur un plan d'image (4) et présentant une forme non axialement symétrique, sont placées de manière excentrique l'une par rapport à l'autre dans le sens du déplacement de la lumière provenant de l'objet. Les sections transversales des première et deuxième faces réflectrices (2, 3) se coupent en un plan comprenant le centre du plan d'image (4), et les sommets des faces réflectrices (2, 3) sont concaves. Par conséquent, la lumière provenant de l'objet est guidée vers le plan d'image (4) sans rencontrer d'obstacle, ce qui permet d'obtenir une bonne image et un dispositif optique réflecteur de grand angle haute performance.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>